nt work also carries obligations beyond the finished artefact. Risks can include unfair contracts, missing credits, opaque accounting, rights conflicts, and unauthorised exploitation. Strong production practice documents ownership, permissions, credits, approvals, and safety responsibilities early enough that they can shape decisions rather than become emergencies.\n\nAccessibility belongs in the same conversation. Captions, audio description, readable graphics, navigable digital interfaces, venue access, and other accommodations can expand who is able to experience the work and can improve clarity for wider audiences.\n\n## What to remember\n\nRecord labels and distribution becomes easier to understand when craft, production systems, audience experience, rights, and safety are treated as connected. The most durable creative organisations learn from each project, document what worked, and improve the process as deliberately as they improve the final work.\n\nThis is an evergreen Blogdel entertainment explainer. Exact rules, contracts, technical standards, and platform requirements can change, so current primary documentation should be checked when a real production decision depends on exact wording.","article_type":"explainer","language":"en","featured_image_url":"/fallback-images/entertainment-fallback-3.png","featured_image_alt":"Record labels and distribution: Why craft matters","word_count":651,"reading_time_minutes":3,"keywords":["entertainment","evergreen","explainer","Record labels and distribution"],"provider":"chatgpt","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","image_source_type":"editorial-fallback","image_provider":"blogdel","image_model":null,"refs":[{"provider":"IFPI","title":"IFPI","url":"https://www.ifpi.org/","authority":"primary","position":0},{"provider":"UNESCO","title":"UNESCO Culture","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/culture","authority":"primary","position":1},{"provider":"WIPO","title":"World Intellectual Property Organization","url":"https://www.wipo.int/copyrig